  "rationale": "The fleet facts are unambiguous: iterative dominates the merged front (14/14 designs, best area 7860 um2), while unrolled_k (best 9189), pipelined (31433) and pipelined_m (19953) contribute nothing to the front. The spec is area-minimisation with a hard 1 MSPS throughput floor and a 2^-10 max-error cap. iterative's shared-datapath, one-rotation-per-cycle structure is the natural low-area candidate; unrolled_k's k chained rotations per cycle add combinational depth and area for a throughput we do not need (iterative already clears 1 MSPS at its Fmax). I therefore concentrate the entire remaining budget on iterative, but tighten the ranges around the accuracy/area knee rather than re-sweeping the full space: data_width 12-16 (below 12 the Q1.(W-2) output cannot represent 2^-10 error; above 16 area grows with little accuracy gain), n_iter 10-16 (the minimum N that reaches 2^-10 max error, plus headroom), and small angle_guard/frac_guard (0-2) since the error budget is already met at modest widths. Keeping both rounding modes lets Optuna trade a handful of gates for accuracy_bits, which is the second hypervolume objective. unrolled_k is dropped from this round because it has 0 front designs and a worse best area; spending budget there would not improve the front or hypervolume."
}

